Source landscape note: the 2023 India economic record around Modi is heavily document-rich in official fiscal/monetary/statistical releases, then supplemented by multilateral surveillance, parliamentary analysis, audits, and Reuters-syndicated local reporting. The strongest discovery clusters are Union Budget/Economic Survey, RBI annual/bulletin materials, MoSPI GDP/CPI releases, IMF Article IV, World Bank India Development Update, OECD India outlook items, CAG audit reports, and a smaller set of English/Hindi news and commentary pieces spanning favorable, mixed, and skeptical framings.

